75
00:04:59,365 --> 00:05:03,979
Next, someone had to check that EMTs
everywhere actually met those standards.

76
00:05:04,029 --> 00:05:10,205
{1}So in nineteen seventy, the National
Registry of Emergency Medical Technicians

77
00:05:10,255 --> 00:05:15,695
was founded, {2}and that's the NREMT,
the same organization whose exam you're

78
00:05:15,745 --> 00:05:22,208
studying for. {3}But standards on
paper don't buy ambulances or radios.

79
00:05:22,258 --> 00:05:27,475
So in nineteen seventy three, the
National EMS Systems Act paid to build

80
00:05:27,525 --> 00:05:32,295
EMS systems across the country, {4}and
it's considered the cornerstone federal

81
00:05:32,345 --> 00:05:33,765
law for EMS systems.

82
00:05:34,265 --> 00:05:37,275
Here's an easy way to
keep the three straight.

83
00:05:37,325 --> 00:05:40,695
{1}Nineteen sixty six set the standards.

84
00:05:40,745 --> 00:05:42,988
{2}Nineteen seventy created the test.

85
00:05:43,038 --> 00:05:47,055
{3}And nineteen seventy
three built the systems.

86
00:05:47,105 --> 00:05:51,884
{4}Then in the early nineteen eighties,
that federal money was folded into

87
00:05:51,934 --> 00:05:57,095
block grants to the states, so control
passed mostly to the states, which

88
00:05:57,145 --> 00:05:59,705
now run their own EMS systems.

89
00:05:59,755 --> 00:06:03,319
{5}But the National Highway Traffic
Safety Administration, NHTSA, which

90
00:06:03,369 --> 00:06:06,545
is part of the DOT,
still provides guidance.

91
00:06:09,595 --> 00:06:12,425
And one of the most useful things
NHTSA gave us is a checklist.

92
00:06:12,475 --> 00:06:15,774
{1}It describes a complete
EMS system with ten standards.

93
00:06:15,824 --> 00:06:19,442
{2}Each one names a part
that the system must have.

94
00:06:19,492 --> 00:06:24,545
{3}And instead of memorizing them as
a list, let's sort them into three

95
00:06:24,595 --> 00:06:27,795
groups and hang each one on Frank's call.

96
00:06:28,295 --> 00:06:31,934
The first group is the
people and the rules.

97
00:06:31,984 --> 00:06:37,149
{1}Regulation and policy means the
laws and rules every system runs under.

98
00:06:37,199 --> 00:06:41,445
{2}Resource management means making
sure everyone has the same equipment

99
00:06:41,495 --> 00:06:46,025
and personnel, so a patient gets the
