199
00:13:17,390 --> 00:13:18,190
go.

200
00:13:18,223 --> 00:13:22,140
So that's why picking the
hospital is a critical decision.

201
00:13:22,190 --> 00:13:26,067
{1}You weigh the patient's condition
against the transport time.

202
00:13:26,117 --> 00:13:30,160
{2}To see that tradeoff clearly, let's
leave Frank for a second and picture

203
00:13:30,210 --> 00:13:33,200
a driver with severe
injuries after a crash.

204
00:13:33,250 --> 00:13:38,440
The closest hospital is five minutes
away, and the trauma center is fifteen.

205
00:13:38,490 --> 00:13:43,032
{3}The closer hospital may have no
surgeon ready, so he might need surgery

206
00:13:43,082 --> 00:13:47,620
that it can't start. {4}But for a
patient who might not survive those extra

207
00:13:47,670 --> 00:13:50,536
ten minutes, the math
can go the other way.

208
00:13:50,586 --> 00:13:54,964
{5}Your local protocols guide this
choice, and they're the rules your medical

